<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅστε</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥτε,
		ὅτε</span> (also written divisim), in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ τε</span></b>  as masc.,
			<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			17.757
		</span></i> : (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς, τε</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>who, which,</i>
			like the simple <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅστις,</span> freq. with a
			generalizing force (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τε</span> is however sts.
			otiose, as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτε, ὥστε, οἷός τε,
				ἐπεί τε,</span> etc., v.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τε</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
				1
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.221
			</span></i>, etc.: neut. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τά τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.481
				</span></i>
			, etc.: pl. fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάς τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.554
				</span></i>
			 : used also in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				2.39
			</span></i>, al., and lyr. passages of Trag. (<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				615
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				151
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tr.</u>
				824
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				445
			</span></i>), but very rare in trim., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				297
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				762
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1024
			</span></i> ; and in Prose only in special forms, such as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅτε, ἐφ᾽ ᾧτε</span> :—rarely
			with antec. expressed, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεάων τάων, αἵ
			τ᾽</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.332
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ ἴκελος, ὅν τ᾽</span> . .
				<i><span class="en">
				24.758
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τά τε φρονέων, ἅ τ᾽ ἐγώπερ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.312
				</span></i>
			.—Not to be confounded with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς τε,</span>
			<i>and who,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.365
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.185
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ οὗτε</span>
			<i>from the</i>
			
			<i>time when</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				762
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ οὗτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
					291.3
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> freq. folld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περ</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τά τε στυγέουσι θεοίπερ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.65
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥα</span> between <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τε</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, αἴγειρος ὥς, ἥ ῥά τε</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				4.483
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				15.411
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.31
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ τε</span>
			<i>in that, because</i>, <i><span class="en">
				1.244
			</span></i>; introducing the reason for making a statement or asking a
			question, <i><span class="en">
				4.32
			</span></i>, al.; so prob. <i><span class="en">
				15.468
			</span></i>: for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅτε, ᾧτε</span>,
			v. sub vocc.: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾇτε</span>, 
				Dor.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾗτε</span>, <i>as</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1308
			</span></i> (lyr.): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ ᾧτε</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
				111.3
			</span></i>.</div>
